d to do so  and joe biden's new proposal  will target offshore profits now and  then this is going to  bigger picture get added into his plan  to require corporations to pay at least  a 15  minimum tax on domestic profits as many  of you know  even though we have a corporate tax rate  here in the united states with no  required minimum tax on corporations the  way individuals have there's something  called the alternative minimum tax  for individuals meaning you can't use  deductions and loopholes  to get down to not owing anything that  in theory that's the point of the  alternative minimum tax  joe biden is proposing something similar  for corporations  on the other side of this is you've got  on one side  a 10 percent tax for offshoring and then  you have a 10  made in america tax credit which you  would qualify for  if you as a business owner revitalize a  closed or almost closed facility  in the united states if you expand a  facility  if you bring some production back to the  united states and there will also be a  ten percent credit available  if you increase manufacturing wages you  it has to be based on pre-coronavirus as  a baseline  up to a hundred thousand dollars this is  super interesting let me give you an  example of how it works  you could conceivably have an employee  earning fifty thousand dollars  and you could say i'm going to give them  a raise to sixty thousand dollars  on that ten thousand dollar raise  biden's proposal is  the government will kick you back ten  percent of it so you give a ten thousand  dollar raise  the government gives you a thousand  dollar tax credit so  you give someone ten thousand dollars it  only costs you nine  that's very very interesting and you  know the macro economic impact  needs to be scored uh but conceptually  it's very interesting  now i i wonder how many of you are  waiting to see whether i will do this  i would be a hypocrite if i didn't point  this out  when joe biden says it because i sure as  hell pointed it out when donald trump  said it  all of the talk about bringing  manufacturing jobs back to the united  states  a lot of these jobs are not coming back  period it doesn't matter if donald trump  is president  it doesn't matter if joe biden is  president and you know a 10  credit here a 10 tax there it's not  going to do it  and that is because the united states  made the decision  implicitly decades ago that we are going  in the direction of being more of a  service-based economy more of a creative  economy  and outsourcing manufacturing to places  where it's cheaper  like china that's the reality and that's  a global reality that's  bigger than 10 tax here or 10 credit  there now that being said if this  incentive got american companies  to for example move a call center back  to the united states  that is much more plausible and i would  find super interesting  for for me one of the biggest customer  service nightmares is when you're trying  to deal with something sensitive for  example  banking payroll airline tickets internet  security  and customer service centers are located  in other parts of the country  which is fine other than when you're  dealing with people that  do not speak english at a certain level  of proficiency that really affects  customer service and when you look at  internet service providers that offshore  call centers when you look at airlines  and all of these others consistently  it destroys the customer experience  we've had recent internet problems  our internet service providers tech  support is in another part of the world  run by mediocre english speakers they're  not bad people they're no worse than  americans  but it is not a great customer service  experience at one point the payroll  company we used to have  had customer service overseas it's not a  great experience to be trying to set up  you know the proper tax deductions for  employees and to have someone where you  don't even know if their english  level is at a level of proficiency where  they're getting what you're trying to do  if this idea gets call centers back in  the united states  that would be super interesting and it  would be really good for a lot of  companies  in any case we're going to continue  tracking joe biden's proposals  this is an interesting one meanwhile  donald trump is doing rallies and  calling joe biden stupid  you decide which approach you prefer i  know which one i prefer
 

